implementationPlan.description:
Ship the edited role doc. packages/moe-daemon/src/generated/initFiles.ts must equal the generate-init-files output for the edited governor.md. The expected diff is exactly 3 one-line hunks, all for governor.md (prototype: /mnt/d/moe-scratch/ed84e283-plan/proto-initFiles.diff):
(1) the ROLE_DOCS['governor.md'] marker changes from `sha=6cedbe83add8` to `sha=c9d4b13ad50b`;
(2) the rubric body line, where backticks are escaped as \\` inside the template literal;
(3) 'c9d4b13ad50b' is inserted in sorted order, right after 'b1c15c152e75', into SHIPPED_ROLE_BODY_SHAS['governor.md']. Keep '6cedbe83add8' in that list so stale marked .moe/roles copies still upgrade.
Apply the hunks with your own Edit tool, for the TOOL witness. A cp back is a shell write, and its path may be HELD at landing. Use the proto only if your worktree base is c54b063b or d1062cb0 (or later with no docs/roles change since) and your governor.md matches proto-doc.diff. Otherwise regenerate: in a clone at base B, follow the step-4 R3 recipe (git clone -q --shared --no-checkout . $S/r; checkout --detach $B; npm ci; overlay the edited doc; npm run -s generate-init-files). Then diff its initFiles.ts against yours and apply each hunk with Edit. Never run npm run build, prebuild, ci or install in the shared checkout or in your worktree. See mem:convention-role-doc-edits-regenerate-initfiles and mem:gotcha-moe-doc-generated-artifacts.
